# __APP_NAME__

A React + Vite front end served by a Node.js + Express server, with data in [Neon](https://neon.tech) serverless Postgres. **One app, one port, one deployable.** There is no separate frontend server.

## Run locally

1. Create a Neon project and copy its connection string (Neon console → **Connect**).
2. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and put the connection string in `DATABASE_URL`.
3. Install, set up the database, start:

```bash
npm install
npm run db:setup   # creates tables, seeds missing rows; safe to re-run
npm run dev        # http://localhost:3000
```

## Deploy

```bash
npm ci && npm run db:setup && npm run build && npm start
```

or deploy to [Render](https://render.com) with the included `render.yaml` (New → Blueprint), or build the included `Dockerfile`. Set the variables below as environment variables / platform secrets. Requires Node 22+.

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | (required) | Neon Postgres connection string |
| `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` | (required) | Signs sessions (`openssl rand -base64 32`) |
| `BETTER_AUTH_URL` | `http://localhost:PORT` | Public origin; set in production |
| `PORT` | `3000` | Port to listen on |
